{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "2021 CKD-EPI Creatinine equation (no race).\n\nFemale, creatinine 0.76 mg/dL. For females, κ = 0.7, α = -0.241.\n\nScr/κ = 0.76/0.7 = 1.0857\n\nSince 0.76 > 0.7, use max term = (1.0857)^(-1.200)\nmin term = 1 (since ratio ≥ 1, min = 1)\n\neGFR = 142 × min(Scr/κ,1)^α × max(Scr/κ,1)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age × 1.012\n\nmin term: (1)^(-0.241) = 1\nmax term: (1.0857)^(-1.200)\n\nln(1.0857) = 0.08224\n× -1.200 = -0.09869\nexp(-0.09869) = 0.90603\n\n0.9938^71:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 71 = -0.44157\nexp = 0.6431\n\nNow multiply:\n142 × 1 × 0.90603 × 0.6431 × 1.012\n\n142 × 0.90603 = 128.66\n× 0.6431 = 82.74\n× 1.012 = 83.73\n\nFINAL: 84"}